  "$schema_note": "Curated whitelist of 'when a user types this, we want that row to lead'. v0.5.3 (#97). Each entry: `query` = the bare noun a user searches; `name_pattern` = case-insensitive ILIKE pattern (may contain % wildcards) that identifies the canonical row(s) in `foods.name`. The rank-foods backfill (scripts/rank-foods.mjs) sets is_canonical=true + rank_penalty=0 on every matching row so the search ORDER BY floats them to the top. Source: USDA SR Legacy + hand-curated portion rows. v1.1 (2026-08-11): patterns rewritten to match actual USDA row names — SR Legacy uses comma-inverted naming like 'Chicken, broilers or fryers, breast, meat only, cooked, roasted' rather than 'Chicken breast, cooked'. Use % wildcards to hit multiple canonical forms; keep patterns narrow enough to avoid junk (canned/babyfood/branded rows).",
